      "text": [
        " بَدَأَنِي أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) مِنْ غَيْرِ أَنْ أَسْأَلَهُ فَقَالَ الِاعْتِكَافُ ثَلَاثَةُ أَيَّامٍ يَعْنِي السُّنَّةَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from dawood Bin Sirhan who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> initiated me from without he asking him<sup>asws</sup>, so he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The <span class=\"iTxt\">Itikaaf</span> is for three days, meaning the Sunnah, Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Willing’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Dawud ibn Sarhan who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, once initiated speaking without my asking anything, ‘’Ttikaf consists of three days, meaning, according to the Sunnah, by the will of Allah.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
